@page "/"

<header>
    <h1>Make your styleguide the default.</h1>
    <p>
        Remove the complexity of CSS-driven HTML by applying your KodeKit styles 
        directly to the semantic HTML. No arbitrary classes, no confusion.
    </p>
    <button @onclick=Go>Start your Style</button>
</header>

<article>
    <section _="on intersection(intersecting) having threshold 0.25
                        if intersecting transition opacity to 1 then set :done to 1
                        else if :done != 1 then transition opacity to 0">
        <header>
            <h4>What is Kodekit?</h4>
        </header>
        <p>
            Kodekit is a new way of building frontend websites & applications.
            The idea is that HTML elements should be styled directly, without
            the need for additional classes. Only adding classes as additional
            modifiers such as style variations and size.
        </p>
        <p>
            Not only that, but Kodekit is also a visual theme builder, meaning
            that you can create your own styleguides & themes visually, without
            writing any css.
        </p>

        <header>
            <h4>Why use this method?</h4>
        </header>
        <p>
            Styling the default HTML directly not only allows for quicker and cleaner
            code, but also allows for more consistency across larger projects.
        </p>
        <p>
            No more chaining together multiple classes to create a primary button, only
            to forget to add some classes every so often.
        </p>

        <button @onclick="@GetStarted">Start Your Style</button>
    </section>
</article>

<section>
    <header>
        <h2>Overview</h2>
        <h3>Introduction</h3>
        <hr />
    </header>
</section>

@code
{
    [CascadingParameter] public Sparc.Blossom.Api.Kit Kit { get; set; } = default!;

    void Go()
    {
        Nav.NavigateTo($"/{Kit.Id}/Colors");
    }
}